cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ZFN WebSuite: repeat-aware, genome-scale design of zinc-finger nucleases with order-ready coding sequences"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: 0.8.1
date-released: "2026-11-19"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/REPLACE_ME/zfn-websuite"
url: "https://zfn.mobilome.cn/"
keywords:
  - zinc finger nuclease
  - ZFN
  - genome editing
  - off-target prediction
  - codon optimization
  - repeat masking
abstract: >-
  A self-contained web server and command-line toolkit that turns a DNA sequence
  or a whole genome into ranked ZFN designs: candidate enumeration, genome-wide
  repeat-aware filtering (RepeatMasker annotation plus genome-wide copy number),
  six-component design scoring, genome-scale off-target burden estimation, and
  fusion-protein construction with humanized coding sequences and an order form.
